codex
Built a native Track-A generator for the paper’s Section 3 \(S=\varnothing\) labeling family.

Local verification passes:

- G1–G9(c) pass.
- Random guessing: 0/200,000.
- Six adversarial attacks: 0/8 successes each.
- Exact DSATUR: 800,008 nodes over eight instances, 49.44 seconds.
- Answer size: 720 characters, 240 elements.
- Determinism, JSON round-trip, corruption rejection, scaling, and canonical-key invariance verified.

Deliverables:

- [Generator module](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1902.05467/gen_1902_05467.py)
- [Self-test report](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1902.05467/selftest_report.json)
- [README](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1902.05467/README.md)
- [Bare transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1902.05467/llm_loop_transcript.jsonl)
- [Structural-hint transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1902.05467/g9_hinted_transcript.jsonl)
- [Placebo-hint transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1902.05467/g9_placebo_transcript.jsonl)

The family uses the paper’s explicit identification of \(S=\varnothing\) labeling with graph coloring. Its Track-A regime is calibrated below the efficient Kesten–Stigum recovery threshold discussed by Abbe–Sandon. [Original paper](https://arxiv.org/abs/1902.05467), [hardness-regime reference](https://arxiv.org/abs/1512.09080).

One external blocker remains: all twelve required OpenRouter redraws returned HTTP 403 `Key limit exceeded`. They are correctly recorded as service errors, not solver failures. Consequently, the result is locally complete but must not be submitted as hardened until the OpenRouter quota is replenished and the three oracle arms are rerun.
