The paper check confirms the exact reduction: Section 3 states \(\lambda_{\varnothing}(G)=2\chi(G)-1\), so the existing problem is genuinely one of the paper’s defined objects. The weak point is narrower: the cited Kesten–Stigum result proves efficient *community detection above* its threshold, not average-case hardness of finding *any* proper coloring below it. I’m stress-testing that gap with stronger available coloring/SAT machinery before deciding whether Track A is honest.
