codex
A concrete attack flaw surfaced: the current “exact DSATUR” fixes only one color name, so it wastes up to \(4!\) branches on globally equivalent label renamings. I’m rerunning the standard search with two endpoint colors anchored (eliminating all \(5\cdot4\) symmetry) and stronger propagation. If that succeeds, the current Track-A claim must be hardened or rejected regardless of the existing report.
