One compliance issue remained in `escalate()`: it declared `cap_bound` at 12 colors even though two harder below-KS regimes still fit the same 240-atom answer. I’m extending the fixed-length ladder through 15 and 16 colors; only after that does maintaining the calibrated regime require increasing \(n\) past the 256-atom cap.
