codex
The generator is built and locally verified, but the required oracle hardening remains externally blocked by OpenRouter quota.

- [Generator](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1902.05467/gen_1902_05467.py:23): Track A, inverse-generated \(S=\varnothing\) oriented \(L(2,1)\)-labelings, grounded in the paper’s Section 3 coloring identity. ([paper](https://arxiv.org/abs/1902.05467))
- [Self-test report](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1902.05467/selftest_report.json): all nine local gates pass.
- [README](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1902.05467/README.md): construction, hardness caveats, example, measurements, and usage.
- [Bare oracle transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1902.05467/llm_loop_transcript.jsonl)
- [Structural-hint transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1902.05467/g9_hinted_transcript.jsonl)
- [Placebo transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1902.05467/g9_placebo_transcript.jsonl)

Key measurements:

- Structure-aware guesses: 0/200,000.
- Seven adversarial attacks: all 0/8.
- Symmetry-normalized DSATUR/DPLL: 800,008 nodes, 43.15 seconds.
- Nonbacktracking spectral attack: 129,893,440 operations, 0/8.
- Answer: 720 characters, 240 atoms; intended route 240 operations.
- Canonicalization: 100/100 invariance and carried-witness checks.

The Track-A calibration uses Abbe–Sandon’s \(O(n\log n)\) ABP theorem above the Kesten–Stigum threshold; the README explicitly notes that being below this threshold is not itself an average-case lower bound. ([Abbe–Sandon](https://arxiv.org/abs/1512.09080))

